     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Home or ambulatory BP monitoring"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " when white coat or masked HTN = sus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "@ dx:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " UA, spot urine albumin:creatinine ratio, creatinine, potassium, sodium, calcium, fasting glucose, lipid panel, TSH and an ECG."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Renal US"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " if UA shows albuminuria, casts or microhematuria, or creatinine or cystatin C = ↑."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "ECG for ♡ effects:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a broad, notched P wave may be an early sign; ↑QRS voltage indicates LVH, which USU prompts an echocardiogram."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Aldosterone and renin"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for hypokalemia ⍉caused by diuretics, and to screen for primary aldosteronism in resistant HTN, OSA or early CVA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Plasma free metanephrines and TSH"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for labile, markedly ↑BP w HA, palpitations, tachy, sweating, tremor or pallor."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
